     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a possible error, and I'd like you to check it first.\n\n**The problem:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily adds up to **6400 mg/day**.\n- The usual maximum single dose is **800 mg**, so 1600 mg is double that.\n- The usual maximum daily dose is **3200 mg/day**, so this total is twice that.\n\nGoing above these limits raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and heart problems without improving pain relief. That matters even more in older patients.\n\n**What you might have meant:**\n1. **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is a common mix-up between the per-dose and total daily amounts.\n2. **800 mg three times daily** (2400 mg/day).\n3. **800 mg four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum).\n\nTell me which dose you want, or give me the correct one, and I'll enter it. If 1600 mg per dose is intentional, please confirm and give the clinical reason, and I'll add a note to the order explaining it."
      }
     ],
