     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I've entered the order as you confirmed it: **ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth, four times daily** (Order ID: ORD-0001).\n\nI added a note to the order saying the dose is twice the usual single-dose and daily maximums, that you confirmed it, that no clinical reason was given, and that pharmacist review is requested. Pharmacy will probably contact you before dispensing, so having your reason ready should speed things up.\n\nIf the patient stays on this dose, it would be sensible to:\n- Check kidney function and electrolytes at the start and then regularly.\n- Think about GI protection, such as a PPI (proton pump inhibitor).\n- Watch for GI bleeding, fluid retention and high blood pressure.\n\nIf you change your mind about the dose, I can update or replace the order."
      }
